        "title": "Show shorter cost comparison periods",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add an opt-in Display setting for shorter 7, 30, and 90-day cost comparisons\n- reuse the selected local-history scan; no additional provider or disk probes\n- show eligible comparison rows in the inline usage dashboard and detailed cost model\n- localize the setting and comparison labels across every shipped app locale\n\nCloses https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/issues/1500\n\nRelated https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/issues/1708 remains open: this does not implement a lifetime ledger.\n\n## Maintainer repair\n\nThe contributor implementation was ported onto current `main`, its stale settings placement was moved into Display, and the runtime path was completed so enabling the setting actually renders the comparison rows. The changelog preserves contributor credit to @jtl06.\n\nExact candidate: `51dbc1a59c3b6a499fd0b53d93cb5c28bda2dfdf`\n\n## Proof\n\n- `swift test --filter MenuCardCostComparisonTests` — 3/3 passed\n- focused cost/history/settings suite — passed\n- `make check` — SwiftFormat, SwiftLint, and 23-locale validation passed\n- `make test` — all 47 shards passed\n- structured autoreview — no accepted or actionable findings; patch-correct confidence 0.86\n- signed Developer ID app, isolated disposable HOME/CODEX_HOME/CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, Keychain access disabled\n- real Display UI persisted the 90-day history and opt-in toggle\n- real menu Refresh rendered `$0.68` / `330K` for 90 days plus `Last 7 days: $0.45 · 220K tokens` and `Last 30 days: $0.45 · 220K tokens`\n- disabling the toggle removed both shorter rows while preserving the 90-day KPIs\n- no `SecurityAgent` prompt; synthetic released-model fixture only; original user preferences restored exactly\n\n## Risk\n\nDefault-off and UI-only. The comparison rows reuse the existing in-memory summary; the main residual risk is extra dashboard height when enabled. A model-level regression covers row eligibility and formatting.\n",
